{"text": "Trends toward a marked increase in competition. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Have forced companies. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To adopt much more aggressive innovation strategies. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovation provides one way. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Of getting out of the competition. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which is to say situations in which activities are not very profitable. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovation indeed provides an opportunity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To set oneself apart. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And temporarily to assume a monopoly position. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This provides an opportunity to make a profit. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Either by increasing prices or by reducing costs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> There are, of course, other means that can be relied upon. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To survive and prosper in a market economy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These conventional means rely mainly on. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Geographical distances and transportation costs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The limited capacity of consumers to compare prices and qualities fully. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And the existence of regulated activities. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> All these mechanisms reduce the degree of competition. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And allow companies to survive. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Even if they do not have. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The best product or the cheapest price. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, globalization, deregulation, and some antitrust policies. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Are all trends. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which dramatically weaken the effectiveness of those conventional means. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovative strategies, therefore, appear as the only way. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To survive and prosper. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In the new competitive environment.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "r", "e", "n", "d", "s", " ", "t", "o", "w", "a", "r", "d", " ", "a", " ", "m", "a", "r", "k", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", "c", 